Makes `Allegrex_ElfExtension` actually win adapter selection for a PSP ELF.

Without this, every PSP import on a Ghidra that also has
`ghidra-emotionengine-reloaded` installed silently loads with **no relocations
applied at all**: the relocation table stays empty, `lui`/`addiu` pairs keep
their pre-relocation immediates and `jal` targets keep base-0 encodings, so
`get_xrefs_to` answers "no references" for functions and data that plainly
have callers. Measured 2026-09-05 against `psp-pulse-usa`; see
docs/ghidra/workflow.md, "Why a PSP import silently loses every relocation".

The mechanism, in four steps, all re-checkable with `javap`:

  1. `ElfExtensionFactory.getLoadAdapter(ElfHeader)` is a plain first-match-wins
     loop over `ClassSearcher.getInstances(ElfExtension.class)`, testing only
     the **one-arg** `canHandle(ElfHeader)`.
  2. `ClassSearcher` orders that list by descending
     `@ExtensionPointProperties(priority)`. `EE_ElfExtension` declares
     `priority = 2`; `Allegrex_ElfExtension` declares nothing, so it gets
     `DEFAULT_PRIORITY = 1` and sorts behind it.
  3. `EE_ElfExtension` overrides only the two-arg `canHandle(ElfLoadHelper)`
     and inherits stock `MIPS_ElfExtension`'s one-arg version, which accepts
     **any** `EM_MIPS` ELF - PSP included.
  4. So the PS2 extension wins the PSP file, and
     `Allegrex_ElfExtension.processGotPlt` - the sole call site of
     `AllegrexRelocationProcessor.process` - never runs. Nothing fails and
     nothing is logged, because nothing is reached.

Note that `Allegrex_ElfExtension`'s existing two-arg
`canHandle(ElfLoadHelper)`, which checks the language is `Allegrex`, is **dead
code for adapter selection** - the factory never calls it. That is why the
language check it performs never prevented any of this, and it is the detail
that otherwise has to be re-derived.

Both hunks are required and neither works alone:

  - Raising the priority alone would make Allegrex win *PS2* ELFs too, the
    exact mirror of the bug being fixed - its one-arg predicate accepts any
    `EM_MIPS` file.
  - Tightening the predicate alone changes nothing, because EE is still tested
    first and still accepts.

The tightened predicate keys on `e_type == 0xffa0` (`ET_PSP_EXEC`), which
holds for all four PSP executables this project uses (`pulse-usa`, `pulse-eu`,
`pure-eu`, `pure-usa` - all `Processor Specific: (ffa0)` per `readelf -h`)
while `pulse-ps2-eu`'s `SCES_547.48` is a plain `EXEC`, so it still falls
through to `EE_ElfExtension`. The `SHT_PSP_REL` section and program-header
scans are a null-guarded fallback for PSP modules reached before `e_type` is
decisive; depending on when the factory runs relative to section parsing they
may be inert, and the `e_type` test is the one that carries the fix.

Applies to ghidra-allegrex commit aec4265, which is what
scripts/build-ghidra-allegrex.sh pins by default.

**Not verified end to end.** The mechanism above is measured; that this patch
removes the symptom follows from it but has not been executed, because doing
so means installing the rebuilt extension into the maintainer's Ghidra and
reimporting the live databases. See
handover/ghidra-psp-relocations-never-applied.md.

--- a/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/extend/Allegrex_ElfExtension.java
+++ b/src/main/java/ghidra/app/util/bin/format/elf/extend/Allegrex_ElfExtension.java
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 import ghidra.program.model.symbol.Symbol;
 import ghidra.program.model.symbol.SymbolUtilities;
 import ghidra.util.Msg;
+import ghidra.util.classfinder.ExtensionPointProperties;
 import ghidra.util.exception.AssertException;
 import ghidra.util.exception.CancelledException;
 import ghidra.util.exception.InvalidInputException;
@@ -53,8 +54,20 @@
 // Note that this class is derived from the MIPS_ElfExtension. When the comment
 // says "PSP relocation section are not supported" it refers to the built-in
 // MIPS plugin, not the Allegrex one.
+// The priority must stay above ghidra-emotionengine-reloaded's EE_ElfExtension
+// (2), which inherits MIPS_ElfExtension's "any EM_MIPS" claim and would
+// otherwise be selected for PSP files, silently skipping every relocation.
+@ExtensionPointProperties(priority = 3)
 public class Allegrex_ElfExtension extends ElfExtension {

+  // e_type of a PSP executable/PRX. PspElfConstants holds the section types,
+  // but they are duplicated here so canHandle stays free of Kotlin interop.
+  private static final int ET_PSP_EXEC = 0xffa0;
+
+  private static final int SHT_PSP_REL = 0x700000a0;
+
+  private static final int SHT_PSP_REL_TYPE_B = 0x700000a1;
+
   private static final String MIPS_STUBS_SECTION_NAME = ".MIPS.stubs";

   // GP value reflected by symbol address
@@ -140,7 +153,36 @@

   @Override
   public boolean canHandle (ElfHeader elf) {
-    return elf.e_machine() == ElfConstants.EM_MIPS;
+    return elf.e_machine() == ElfConstants.EM_MIPS && isPsp(elf);
+  }
+
+  // Claim only PSP files. Being selected for a PS2 ELF would be the same bug
+  // this class's raised priority exists to fix, pointing the other way.
+  private static boolean isPsp (ElfHeader elf) {
+    if ((elf.e_type() & 0xffff) == ET_PSP_EXEC) {
+      return true;
+    }
+    ElfSectionHeader[] sections = elf.getSections();
+    if (sections != null) {
+      for (ElfSectionHeader section : sections) {
+        if (isPspRelocationType(section.getType())) {
+          return true;
+        }
+      }
+    }
+    ElfProgramHeader[] headers = elf.getProgramHeaders();
+    if (headers != null) {
+      for (ElfProgramHeader header : headers) {
+        if (isPspRelocationType(header.getType())) {
+          return true;
+        }
+      }
+    }
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  private static boolean isPspRelocationType (int type) {
+    return type == SHT_PSP_REL || type == SHT_PSP_REL_TYPE_B;
   }

   @Override
